Task: Wire the keyboard gate into CI
Phase: 5 (Browser Verification & Release)
Scope: .github/workflows/ci.yml, package.json

The suite-wide playwright run already picks the keyboard specs up now that
testDir covers tests/, but that alone does not satisfy the ci-pipeline spec
delta, which requires the gate to fail rather than degrade into a passing skip
if the spec file goes missing.

Named explicitly as its own step so deletion or a rename produces 'No tests
found' and exit 1. Confirmed empirically against a nonexistent path rather than
assumed - the first attempt to check this read the exit code of tail through a
pipe and wrongly reported 0.

Visual regression confirmed unaffected in the same phase: 30 of 30 pass with no
baseline updates, satisfying the delta's requirement that accessibility changes
leave rendered output unchanged.
